invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_switch_version takes a switch after a CRYPTO byte from the
  server arrived. The server sends every CRYPTO frame in the negotiated
  version, and one in the original version makes the original the
  negotiated one (rfc9369.txt:236-244), so the switch derives keys under
  a version the server did not use. test/quic_version_tests.h delivers
  one byte of the ServerHello and requires CH_EINVAL, with the session
  still waiting for the ServerHello.

--- old
           q->step == HSQ_STEP_AWAIT_SERVER_HELLO && q->t.pt_len == 0 &&
--- new
           q->step == HSQ_STEP_AWAIT_SERVER_HELLO &&
